{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777467135,"nonce":"5wKYTLE+EpqOFoUkfouCuZH5Yq8=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABA1H8UA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/103","origin":"github"},"title":"feat(bizzyboat): bring SBG Ellipse-D into ROS on gabby via PORT_E (RTCM forward + nav logging)","message":"## Goal\n\nBring the SBG Ellipse-D INS into ROS on **gabby** via the SBG's **PORT_E**, so that:\n\n1. SBG nav/IMU data is published under `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/...` and bag-recorded for offline parity comparison against the FCU's solution (`/bizzy/mavros/...`).\n2. RTCM corrections from the existing NTRIP client (currently feeding only the FCU as `mavros_msgs/RTCM` on `/bizzy/mavros/gps_rtk/send_rtcm`) are also forwarded to the SBG's internal GNSS via the ECom link, enabling RTK on the SBG.\n\nQINSy on mercat keeps using PORT_A — gabby's connection on PORT_E is independent, full-duplex, and supported by the firmware.\n\n## Background\n\n- The official `sbg_ros2_driver` (vendor-maintained, available as `ros-jazzy-sbg-driver` from apt) supports RTCM input natively: subscribes to `rtcm_msgs/Message` and forwards bytes to the SBG's internal GNSS over the ECom link. No custom node needed for RTCM injection.\n- The existing NTRIP client (`ntrip_client` from LORD-MicroStrain, configured in `bizzyboat_project11/launch/ntrip_launch.py`) publishes `mavros_msgs/RTCM` directly into mavros. Since `mavros_msgs/RTCM` and `rtcm_msgs/Message` are different ROS types (same RTCM3 payload, different field name and package), a small relay node is needed to feed the SBG driver without disturbing the FCU pipeline.\n- Sensor topic-namespace convention in `bizzyboat_project11` is `sensors/\u003cname\u003e` (see `sensors/ntrip`, `sensors/deltat`, `sensors/cameras`). SBG follows the same pattern: `sensors/sbg`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- [ ] **Apt dependency**: add `\u003cexec_depend\u003esbg_driver\u003c/exec_depend\u003e` to `bizzyboat_project11/package.xml` so rosdep picks up `ros-jazzy-sbg-driver` on fresh hosts.\n- [ ] **New `bizzyboat_project11/config/sbg_ellipse_d.yaml`** (driver config for gabby's PORT_E):\n  - `confWithRos: false` — sbgCenter owns device config, gabby's driver only consumes streams. Avoids fighting QINSy/mercat over device-global settings.\n  - `uartConf.portID: 4` (PORT_E), `portName` and baud rate set per cable (placeholder `/dev/ttyUSB?` until cabled).\n  - `rtcm.subscribe: true`; set `rtcm.namespace: \"\"` and `rtcm.topic_name: \"rtcm\"` so the driver subscribes to `\u003cnode_namespace\u003e/rtcm` = `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/rtcm`.\n- [ ] **New `bizzyboat_project11/scripts/rtcm_relay_node.py`**:\n  - Sub: `mavros_msgs/RTCM` on `/bizzy/mavros/gps_rtk/send_rtcm`.\n  - Pub: `rtcm_msgs/Message` on `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/rtcm`.\n  - Body: copy `header`, copy `data` -\u003e `message`. ~15 lines.\n  - Match the executable-script pattern used by `ntrip_diagnostics_node.py` and friends.\n- [ ] **New `bizzyboat_project11/launch/sbg_launch.py`**:\n  - `PushRosNamespace('sensors/sbg')` (matches existing convention).\n  - Run `sbg_device` node from `sbg_driver` package with the new YAML.\n  - Run `rtcm_relay_node.py`.\n- [ ] **Wire `sbg_launch.py` into `core_launch.py`** as an `IncludeLaunchDescription`, after the existing `ntrip_launch.py` include.\n- [ ] **`bizzyboat_project11/setup.py` / `CMakeLists.txt`** updated to install the new script and launch file (whichever build system the package uses).\n\n## Decisions locked\n\n- **Device-config authority**: sbgCenter (one-time, manual). Driver runs `confWithRos: false`. Avoids QINSy\u003c-\u003egabby drift.\n- **Topic namespace**: `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/...` (matches `sensors/ntrip`, `sensors/deltat`, `sensors/cameras`).\n- **SBG vs FCU comparison**: bag both topics; live-diff node deferred to a follow-up.\n- **SBG-flow diagnostics node**: deferred (matches `ntrip_diagnostics` / `gps_rtk_diagnostics` pattern, but out of this PR's scope).\n\n## Out of scope (follow-up issues)\n\n- Live SBG-vs-FCU diff/comparison node.\n- SBG-flow diagnostics node.\n- PPS splitter cable for the M3 sonar — unrelated to UART wiring (PPS rides on a SYNC_OUT pin, not on PORT_A or PORT_E). Will need its own hardware-and-config issue.\n- Any change to QINSy's PORT_A configuration.\n\n## Verification\n\n- [ ] `ros-jazzy-sbg-driver` resolves via rosdep on a clean host.\n- [ ] Driver comes up against gabby's PORT_E and publishes under `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/...`.\n- [ ] Topic paths confirmed to match `sensors/\u003cname\u003e` convention.\n- [ ] `ros2 topic hz /bizzy/sensors/sbg/rtcm` matches `/bizzy/mavros/gps_rtk/send_rtcm` rate.\n- [ ] SBG GNSS reaches RTK-FIXED with NTRIP active.\n- [ ] Bag-record session captures both `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/...` and `/bizzy/mavros/...` for offline parity check.\n- [ ] QINSy on mercat (PORT_A) is unaffected throughout.\n\n## Field prerequisites (must be confirmed before bench/field test, not blocking PR)\n\n- Cable harness exposes PORT_E (Ellipse-D's standard Master Cable typically only breaks out PORT_A + PORT_B + sync — PORT_E often requires a junction-box variant or custom breakout).\n- Output messages on PORT_E enabled in sbgCenter once before gabby will see anything (consequence of `confWithRos: false`).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}